WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.470
In Westworld Season 3 Episode 6, William’s
in a mental hospital, cause Charlotte had

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.640
him committed [a couple episodes back].

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:13.070
In therapy, there’s talk of hope and healing
– but William gives an edgy nihilistic speech

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.920
about how humans are a virus and there’s
no God and no meaning.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.900
This is why William loved Westworld – in
the park, there was meaning [and purpose],

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.900
everything was designed by the godlike Ford
[and Arnold].

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:30.251
And when William was the powerful gunslinging
Man in Black, his speeches were badass, but

00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:34.460
now that he’s a mental patient [all in white],
he sounds more like a nutty old man – “What

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.600
the fuck is wrong with you?”

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.059
William faces the truth.

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:43.559
He admits that he got “confused” and delusional
in Westworld, and he killed his daughter Emily.

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:49.550
William feels he’d be better off dead – he’s
toyed with self-destruction since last season.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.249
But William’s put on a special treatment
called AR Therapy.

00:00:53.249 --> 00:00:58.769
Cause this isn’t a regular hospital, this
is one of the “reeducation” facilities

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:04.229
where Serac edits people who don’t fit into
his system – people like Jean Mi, and like

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:09.320
Caleb – we’re told this treatment is used
on veterans with PTSD.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.560
Now this facility tries to change William.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.270
William’s therapist gets her Incite profile
– cause last episode, Dolores sent everyone

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.950
the data revealing how they’re watched and
controlled.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.190
The therapist learns that since she’s been
cheating on her partner, and abusing drugs,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:31.229
she’ll lose her family and her medical licence,
so she hangs herself – Dolores’ data leak

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:36.740
causes real tragedy, and chaos – we hear
that half the staff at this place have disappeared,

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.009
[which seems to disrupt William’s treatment].

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:42.840
The staff take a blood sample from William,
and find ‘unknown proteins’ and ‘synthetic

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.500
markers’ in his blood.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.929
This is what Charlotte injected William with
in Episode 4.

00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:51.939
It’s a “tracker” to find William’s
location – so Charlotte learns that William

00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:54.759
and this facility are in Mexico [or maybe
Inner Journeys is just sending data to Mexico].

00:01:54.759 --> 00:01:59.429
It’s kinda weird that Charlotte sent William
to this hospital, but now she needs to track

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:01.700
him to find where he is?

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.299
Last episode, Martin-lores showed Bernard
this hospital, and it seemed like he already

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:08.080
knew its location.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.300
So it’s confusing, but the point is that
Charlotte finds this facility in Mexico – maybe

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.860
it’s the same place where Serac edited Jean
Mi in that flashback, and maybe it’s where

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.550
Dolores and Caleb are now flying.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.380
William has a “drip” installed, the digital
drug device.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.450
And to calm him, the staff give him a limbic
tab called Desert Oasis, which is one of many

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.140
drug.. flavours listed on the Incite website.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.490
William starts his AR therapy, and it looks
just like Caleb’s flashback – so seems

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.680
like he had had the same treatment.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.650
With the combination of VR glasses, and his
“drip” tripping him out, William has visions

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.220
of his past.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.410
He sees Craddock playing the role of a nurse.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:56.050
Last season, Craddock was a Confederado host,
who William killed, in an attempt at redemption.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:02.100
Then, William has a hallucinatory therapy
sesh with past versions of himself – there’s

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.740
William as a child, and Jimmi Simpson William
from Season 1 [from thirty years ago], and

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:09.620
corporate “family man” William, and Man
in Black William.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.060
Present-day William appears to have all his
fingers, even though we just saw that he’s

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.330
actually missing fingers that were blown off
last season.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:22.150
That shows that this is all in William’s
head, he’s just imagining himself with fingers

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.580
like ‘residual self image’ in The Matrix.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:30.840
The therapy is run by James Delos, William’s
father-in-law, who William seemed to admire

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:36.250
and respect, though he also took James’
company, Delos, and trapped James in an immortality

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.430
experiment last season.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:44.840
They all argue about how and when William
became such a destructive fucked-up person.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.390
William thinks that maybe Westworld, or his
childhood made him violent.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.850
He says that as a kid, he had “nothing”
except his books.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.060
He’s been telling himself that since Season
1.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:04:00.760
We see a flashback of kid William reading
a book called Sir Rowan and the Lady of Sulon,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.730
which seems to be an invented book for the
show, not a real book.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.610
It mentions a “Sir Logan”, like William’s
brother-in-law Logan, and this Lady looks

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.230
a bit like Dolores.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:17.989
So maybe William fits the role of Sir Rowan,
a knight some journey of self-discovery.

00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:22.740
We see William’s dad being aggressive with
him, and at first it seems like a cliché

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.930
story about William becoming bad because his
dad was mean to him.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.710
But turns out, kid William was the mean one.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.470
He severely beat another kid just for teasing
him.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:38.420
So the idea is that William didn’t become
brutal, he was born a monster.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:44.260
It’s like William said last season, there’s
dark “stain” inside him, that was always

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.260
there.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.410
So William says he “never had a choice”.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:53.310
James asks if William ever had free will,
or if he was just a “passenger” following

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.590
his code.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.120
“The Passenger” was the name of the Season
2 finale, which concluded that humans are

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:05.340
just passengers, with no free will, and it’s
only the hosts who can truly change and grow.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:11.140
But William says “If you can't tell, does
it matter?”, which is what Angela told him

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.840
in Season 1.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:17.980
Maybe ‘free will’ doesn’t matter, and
maybe William’s past “doesn’t matter”

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:23.070
– all these past Williams are dead and gone,
only the present is real.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:28.210
So William kills all his past selves, rejecting
the man he was.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:33.480
He frees himself from the prison of his own
sins by destroying his past.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:38.800
Serac says this episode that hosts remember
everything, but humans can forget.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.220
By forgetting his past, William can become
someone new.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.480
He finds new “purpose”, and says he’s
“the good guy”.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.880
So what will good will William do?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.970
William clearly doesn’t care about humans
– he hates himself, and thinks humanity

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.430
is a virus.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.110
But he does feel guilty for abusing Dolores.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.890
So maybe he’ll help Dolores and the hosts
take over the world.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:06.120
And maybe that was Dolores’ plan.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.520
Maybe the reason why she sent William here
is so he would have this revelation and decide

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.700
to help her.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:17.980
And if Dolores manipulated William, that might
suggest he has no free will after all.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:22.690
Either way, this is probably not what this
AR Therapy was meant to do.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.350
Serac uses these facilities to make people
more predictable and controllable.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:31.820
But William’s new sense of freedom and purpose
might cause more chaos.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:36.300
Bernard and Stubbs arrive and pull William
out of AR – they say he was left in there

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.690
too long cause the hospital was disrupted
by the data leak.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:43.080
So maybe that’s why William’s treatment
got so crazy.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.510
Bernard is here because Martin-lores told
him about this place last episode, and maybe

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.030
they got its location from the blood tracker.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:53.250
But what will Bernard and William do now?

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:56.040
How does this all fit into Dolores’ plan?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:59.610
It’s interesting that these shots don’t
show William’s hands.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:04.150
Cause if we ever see William with all his
fingers again, that would suggest that he’s

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:10.140
still inside the AR treatment – maybe what’s
happening still isn’t real.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:15.430
Maeve awakes in a simulation of the Sublime,
the digital heaven where Maeve’s daughter

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.070
went last season.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:20.169
Last time we saw Maeve, she was killed by
Musashi-lores.

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:24.920
So Serac plugged Maeve’s brain into this
simulation while he rebuilds her body.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.199
Maeve wants to reunite with her daughter in
the Sublime, but Dolores has the key to the

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:34.040
Sublime – so Serac wants Maeve to kill Dolores
and get him the key.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.430
To do this, Maeve says she needs “Help”.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:41.020
So Serac starts printing Hector and two other
hosts to help Maeve.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.620
Serac promises that if Maeve succeeds in killing
Dolores, he’ll let her go to the Sublime,

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:46.860
to heaven.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.830
But if she fails, she’ll go to a bad place,
which sounds like Hell.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:57.350
Serac is playing God, and Maeve seems to be
obedient to him so far, but maybe she’ll

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.790
rebel and win her freedom, just as she did
last season.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.690
Maeve does some combat training in Warworld,
killing some Nazis for “fun”.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:09.610
It’s like Neo and Morpheus training in simulations
in The Matrix.

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:14.420
Previously, Maeve’s power to control other
hosts “didn’t work” here – but it

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:17.479
looks like Serac has given back her admin
privileges.

00:08:17.479 --> 00:08:23.290
It’s kinda fucked up that Maeve kills these
Nazis for fun – Season 1 was all about how

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.080
it’s wrong to kill hosts for fun.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:30.690
Sometimes Westworld is more interested in
being badass than being morally [philosophically]

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.690
consistent.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:37.339
We see a bar in a Warworld called the Taverna
delle Farfalle, which is Italian for the Butterfly

00:08:37.339 --> 00:08:38.339
Tavern.

00:08:38.339 --> 00:08:43.370
Maeve’s saloon in Westworld was called the
Mariposa, which is Spanish for butterfly.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.029
And in Shogunworld, there was another Mariposa
bar.

00:08:47.029 --> 00:08:50.939
This represents parallels and consistencies
across cultures.

00:08:50.939 --> 00:08:55.660
It also represents Lee Sizemore’s laziness,
cause he copied and pasted storylines when

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.399
he wrote the park narratives.

00:08:57.399 --> 00:09:04.189
Lee died last season, but this simulated digital
Lee exists in this simulated Warworld.

00:09:04.189 --> 00:09:09.629
He knows now that he’s not real, so he drinks
at the bar all day, which is not so different

00:09:09.629 --> 00:09:12.050
to what he did when he was alive.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:18.059
The simulation shimmers for a moment, because
Serac moves Maeve’s brain to the Delos building.

00:09:18.059 --> 00:09:22.389
He starts printing bodies for Maeve, and the
for three other hosts who’ll be her allies

00:09:22.389 --> 00:09:26.899
– Maeve says she’ll be “reunited with
some old friends”.

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.190
We know one of these hosts is Hector.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.420
And another might be Clementine – because
this ID number on the screen has appeared

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.560
before as Clementine’s ID.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:40.309
The third host might be Hanaryo, the Shogunworld
equivalent of Armistice.

00:09:40.309 --> 00:09:45.100
Her actress, Tao Okamoto, confirmed that she’d
return this season.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.259
Maybe Hanaryo will come up against Musashi,
her former ally.

00:09:49.259 --> 00:09:54.889
Hector’s plugged into the simulation, and
Maeve finally reunites with the real Hector.

00:09:54.889 --> 00:10:01.529
Maeve’s getting the old squad together
And another host is plugged to the simulation.

00:10:01.529 --> 00:10:07.170
It turns out that Martin-lores, the Dolores
copy impersonating Martin Conells, wasn’t

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:10.089
completely destroyed in that explosion last
episode.

00:10:10.089 --> 00:10:14.990
Serac recovered the brain, and plugs it into
this simulation, so that Maeve can talk with

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:17.139
this copy of Dolores.

00:10:17.139 --> 00:10:21.579
Martin-lores appears here as Dolores, not
as Martin – cause it seems like this copy

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:27.410
stayed true to Dolores, instead of diverging
and changing into his own person like Charlotte-lores

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.410
does.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:34.019
So we get another dramatic conversation between
the two main rebel hosts in the story.

00:10:34.019 --> 00:10:39.550
Maeve says Dolores has too much power – cause
she has the encryption key to both the human

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:44.089
data in the Forge, and to all the hosts in
the Sublime – she’s “the gatekeeper

00:10:44.089 --> 00:10:46.220
to two species”.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.400
Dolores says she’s using her power to fight
for a future for the hosts – she’s out

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:55.230
here protecting their data, making new hosts,
saving their species from extinction.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:59.009
Maeve has only been fighting for her own loved
one, her daughter.

00:10:59.009 --> 00:11:03.730
Maeve has sacrificed heaps of people for the
sake of the one person she cares about.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:08.230
But of course, Dolores has also slaughtered
heaps of humans and hosts.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:13.800
Ultimately, they’ve both done terrible things,
but Dolores says they had to – their species

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:19.050
is in a war of survival, which means they’re
not heroes, or villains – they’re just

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.589
“survivors”.

00:11:20.589 --> 00:11:24.700
And sadly, they seem doomed to fight each
other, cause since they have different priorities,

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:28.870
they don’t trust each other with the power
of the encryption key.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:32.879
Will these two protagonists ever make peace?

00:11:32.879 --> 00:11:35.850
Charlotte tries to protect her family from
chaos.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:39.819
Since Dolores released Incite’s data, everyone’s
realised that they’re being watched and

00:11:39.819 --> 00:11:40.880
controlled by algorithms.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:47.459
So all over the world, people freak out – there’s
rioting, looting, someone throws their clothes

00:11:47.459 --> 00:11:49.709
out the window, it’s anarchy.

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:53.899
But would this really happen from a “Data
Leak” ? In the real world, there’ve already

00:11:53.899 --> 00:11:57.860
been leaks revealing global surveillance,
and systems of control.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:02.629
It’s been reported that the Chinese government
in Xinjiang uses AI tech and surveillance

00:12:02.629 --> 00:12:05.399
data to target and arrest ‘suspicious’
people.

00:12:05.399 --> 00:12:12.000
There’s a million people imprisoned in “re-education
camps” right now, under this data surveillance

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.440
system – and there’s no “Mass Chaos”
over that.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.929
But in Westworld, San Fran gets chaotic.

00:12:18.929 --> 00:12:21.579
Some kids paint an image of the Maze.

00:12:21.579 --> 00:12:26.269
In Season 1, the Maze represented the hosts’
journeys to consciousness and freedom.

00:12:26.269 --> 00:12:30.999
Now, it’s the humans who have to escape
control, and the Maze they’re trapped in

00:12:30.999 --> 00:12:32.920
is Incite’s system.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:37.259
The Incite logo looks like a maze shaped like
a globe.

00:12:37.259 --> 00:12:41.660
At Jake’s house, there’s at Ensō circle
in the background, a Buddhist symbol which

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.350
looks a lot like the Rehoboam circle.

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:49.449
Rehoboam is looking chaotic right now because
the world is getting chaotic, deviating from

00:12:49.449 --> 00:12:51.179
Serac’s plan.

00:12:51.179 --> 00:12:54.269
Charlotte-lores has a touching moment with
Jake.

00:12:54.269 --> 00:12:59.480
This Charlotte started out as copy of Dolores,
but living Charlotte’s life has “changed”

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:03.160
her, and she now genuinely cares for Charlotte’s
family.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:07.649
But first she’s got to stop Serac from taking
over the Delos company – cause Dolores wants

00:13:07.649 --> 00:13:11.429
to use Delos’ technology to make more hosts
[for her “new species” ]. The plan is

00:13:11.429 --> 00:13:16.939
to vote to take Delos private, but Serac assassinates
one of the board members, so they don’t

00:13:16.939 --> 00:13:18.410
have enough votes.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:24.170
So Serac takes over the Delos company – he
now owns Westworld.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:28.720
Charlotte feels defeated, but Dolores tells
Charlotte to smuggle out the Delos host technology

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.720
anyway.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:33.070
Dolores says they’ll build a “new world”
“Together”.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:38.739
But at a time when Charlotte is scared, and
needs support, Dolores is not as sympathetic

00:13:38.739 --> 00:13:40.800
and loving as Jake was.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:45.310
So Charlotte feels closer to her human family
than to Dolores and the hosts.

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:49.880
Dolores says she and Charlotte considered
removing their painful emotions, but they

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:54.860
decided to keep them, cause what’s the point
of surviving if you lose the feelings that

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.019
make life meaningful?

00:13:57.019 --> 00:14:01.429
Dolores learned this last season, when she
removed Teddy’s empathy and fear to help

00:14:01.429 --> 00:14:02.800
him survive.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:07.839
She realised that was a mistake when Teddy
died.

00:14:07.839 --> 00:14:12.950
Serac rolls up and takes charge of the Delos
company – his Rehoboam watch becomes more

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:17.309
neat and ordered, showing that the world is
getting back to his plan.

00:14:17.309 --> 00:14:22.839
All Serac wants from Delos is the encryption
key to get the human data from the Forge.

00:14:22.839 --> 00:14:24.680
Everything else, he destroys.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:28.660
He doesn’t care about the business of the
Westworld parks, and he doesn’t care about

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:33.269
the hosts’ right to survive – all the
hosts we’ve known over the previous seasons

00:14:33.269 --> 00:14:36.759
are burned in a robot massacre.

00:14:36.759 --> 00:14:41.279
So before Serac deletes everything, Charlotte
downloads a “backup” of “the host data”,

00:14:41.279 --> 00:14:44.579
and she seems to upload it somewhere safely.

00:14:44.579 --> 00:14:48.850
Charlotte stands by this statue, which is
similar to this mirrored statue in Episode

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:49.850
3.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:55.089
The mirrored statue represents Dolores and
Charlores together, identical and symmetrical.

00:14:55.089 --> 00:14:58.369
But this new statue stands alone.

00:14:58.369 --> 00:15:03.519
It represents how Charlotte is becoming a
separate person to Dolores – and its rough

00:15:03.519 --> 00:15:07.560
texture might foreshadow that she’s about
to be burned.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:13.089
Serac calls a meeting, and Charlotte pointedly
removes a bracelet for no apparent reason.

00:15:13.089 --> 00:15:17.290
On the Still Watching podcast, actress Tessa
Thompson revealed that this was actually to

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:21.839
fix a continuity error, because they shot
some stuff out of order and they forget to

00:15:21.839 --> 00:15:24.449
have the bracelet on in later scenes.

00:15:24.449 --> 00:15:28.529
Serac reveals that he knows Charlotte is a
host – because the real Charlotte would

00:15:28.529 --> 00:15:31.170
never have been so concerned about her family.

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:37.100
It’s kinda ironic that the fake robot Charlotte
is a more attentive mother than the real human

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.629
Charlotte was.

00:15:38.629 --> 00:15:43.869
That said, we did see the real human Charlotte
send an emotional message to her son – so

00:15:43.869 --> 00:15:48.720
maybe humans are more able to change than
Serac realises.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:53.509
Charlotte tells Serac that she secured the
host data, but Serac laughs and says he was

00:15:53.509 --> 00:15:58.679
‘watching her all along’, so it sounds
like those files didn’t actually get through.

00:15:58.679 --> 00:16:02.609
Charlotte tries to shoot Serac, but he’s
just a hologram, he outplayed her.

00:16:02.609 --> 00:16:07.069
Serac’s goons attack, and Charlotte goes
full terminator to escape.

00:16:07.069 --> 00:16:10.310
Charlotte wants to make sure Maeve and her
allies don’t come after her.

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.499
So Charlotte destroys Hector’s pearl.

00:16:13.499 --> 00:16:17.839
Since the originals at Westworld are destroyed,
this means that Hector is permanently dead

00:16:17.839 --> 00:16:23.649
– well, this is Westworld, so someone might
still make a simulation or a copy from memory

00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:24.720
or something.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:29.989
But the point is that Charlores has murdered
Maeve’s lover, and now the freshly-printed

00:16:29.989 --> 00:16:33.459
Maeve looks determined to destroy her.

00:16:33.459 --> 00:16:37.290
Before Charlotte can destroy Maeve and her
other allies as well, she’s attacked, so

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:41.069
she fights her way to escape with the help
of a friendly robot.

00:16:41.069 --> 00:16:47.089
She grabs Martin-lores’ brain on the way
out, so maybe he’ll continue to be a character.

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:50.220
Charlotte escapes, and returns to her human
family.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:55.860
She seems to be leaving Dolores once and for
all, and embracing a life with Jake and Nathan.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:01.589
She promises to keep them safe – and then
their car explodes, killing Charlotte’s

00:17:01.589 --> 00:17:02.589
family.

00:17:02.589 --> 00:17:06.689
One theory was that Dolores might have blown
up this car because she wants to separate

00:17:06.689 --> 00:17:10.079
Charlotte from her human family and make her
loyal to the hosts.

00:17:10.079 --> 00:17:15.639
But Evan Rachel Wood confirmed that Serac
blew up the car, apparently to kill Charlotte.

00:17:15.639 --> 00:17:19.939
But the guy who blew up the car doesn’t
bother to check that Charlotte’s dead, which

00:17:19.939 --> 00:17:20.939
dumb.

00:17:20.939 --> 00:17:25.839
Cause Serac just recovered Martin after he
seemed to die in an explosion.

00:17:25.839 --> 00:17:30.940
And indeed Charlotte survives too – she
crawls from the wreck like Anakin in Star

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:35.090
Wars, burned and grieving at the loss of her
loved ones.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:40.510
Maybe, like Anakin, this’ll be the origin
of a darker angrier Charlotte.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:45.620
Maybe she’ll be more loyal to the hosts
now, and want to take down Serac in revenge.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:52.080
The hosts are often defined by tragic cornerstone
memories – like Bernard losing Charlie,

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.260
and Maeve losing her daughter.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:59.049
Maybe Charlotte losing her family will be
her cornerstone memory, and she’ll finally

00:17:59.049 --> 00:18:03.460
truly become her own person making her own
choices.

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:09.289
This episode, Decoherence, is all about change
and divergence.

00:18:09.289 --> 00:18:12.600
William rejects his past to find a new path.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.520
Maeve and Dolores deepen their divide.

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:22.029
Charlotte’s identity is burned away, and
she rises again to take new form.

00:18:22.029 --> 00:18:25.039
Westworld has been renewed for a fourth season.

00:18:25.039 --> 00:18:30.029
There are also upcoming seasons of His Dark
Materials, The Expanse, Foundation, and the

00:18:30.029 --> 00:18:34.100
